api_examples:
Example: non-streaming usage (generated types + zod):

// Generated types and zod are available from the shape bundle
import { Client } from '@redwood/ts-client';
import { MyThing, MyThingSchema } from '@redwood/ts-client/schemas/my-thing';

const c = new Client({ enableOutputValidation: 'warn' });
const out = await c.generate<{ result: MyThing }>(prompt);
const parsed = MyThingSchema.parse(out.result); // throws if mismatch; otherwise typed MyThing

Streaming example: progressive parsing of a discriminated union:

import { streamingParse } from '@redwood/ts-client/streaming';
import { MyStreamSchema } from '@redwood/ts-client/schemas/my-stream';

const stream = await c.stream(prompt, { model: 'x' });
for await (const chunk of streamingParse(stream, MyStreamSchema)) {
  if (chunk.type === 'partial') {
    // partial validation passed up to the discriminator, keep aggregating
  } else if (chunk.type === 'complete') {
    // validated final object available as chunk.value
  } else if (chunk.type === 'error') {
    // handle validation error
  }
}

Notes: streamingParse accepts discriminatorHint callbacks to decide union branch early and avoid validating against all branches. The generated schema exports a small `discriminatorHints()` helper for this purpose.
